===============================================================================
THE MANIFEST — write this even if you finish nothing else
===============================================================================

MANIFEST.md, and it is the most important file you produce. A dataset I cannot
trust the boundaries of is worse than no dataset.

  1. Every file written, with its row count, and complete / lower-bound /
     partial / empty-on-purpose for each.
  2. excluded_under_directive: <n>. Nothing else about those rows.
  3. Every field you stripped for rule 3, named.
  4. Every endpoint that failed, capped, or returned nothing — with the query,
     the cap, and whether "nothing" means empty or means blocked. Truncated
     windows listed individually.
  5. The three Tier 0 numbers on their own lines: account created_at,
     tweet_count, followers_count.
  6. The true 2025 post count, on its own line.
  7. Anything you found that I did not ask for and that looks like it matters.
  8. What a full Settings-export zip would still add that the API cannot give,
     so I know what remains worth requesting later.

If you have to choose: completeness of item 02 beats everything below it, and
an honest boundary beats a full-looking file every single time.
